## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Newton's method)
## KEYWORDS("Newton's method", 'rootfinding')
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## MLT(Newton-f-value)
## Level(2)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('4.1')
## Problem1('7')
#Problem APEX 4.1.7

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');
Context('Numeric')->flags->set(tolerance => 0.00001, tolType => "absolute");

@x = (random(2, 2.7, 0.1));

$f  = Formula("ln(x)");
$df = $f->D('x');

for my $k (0 .. 4) {
    push(@x, $x[$k] - $f->eval(x => $x[$k]) / $df->eval(x => $x[$k]));
}

BEGIN_PGML
Use 5 iterations of Newton's Method 
with the given initial approximation to approximate
the root of the function.  All answers should be given
to 5 decimal digits of accuracy.

[```  
   f(x) = \ln x, \qquad x_0 = [$x[0]]
```] 

- [` x_1 = `] [_]{$x[1]}{30}
- [` x_2 = `] [_]{$x[2]}{30}
- [` x_3 = `] [_]{$x[3]}{30}
- [` x_4 = `] [_]{$x[4]}{30}
- [` x_5 = `] [_]{$x[5]}{30}

END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Set up the iterative formula for Newton's Method:
[```
  x_{n+1} = x_n - \dfrac{f(x_n)}{f'(x_n)} 
  = x_n - \dfrac{\ln x_n}{\frac{1}{x_n}} 
  = x_n - x_n \ln x_n
```]

The iterations are
[```
  \begin{aligned}
    x_0 &= [$x[0]] \\
    x_1 &= [$x[0]] - ([$x[0]])\ln([$x[0]]) \approx [$x[1]] \\
    x_2 &= [$x[1]] - ([$x[1]])\ln([$x[1]]) \approx [$x[2]] \\
    x_3 &= [$x[2]] - ([$x[2]])\ln([$x[2]]) \approx [$x[3]] \\
    x_4 &= [$x[3]] - ([$x[3]])\ln([$x[3]]) \approx [$x[4]] \\
    x_5 &= [$x[4]] - ([$x[4]])\ln([$x[4]]) \approx [$x[5]]
  \end{aligned}
```]
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();    

